Hi,

At Wed, 05 Jun 2002 09:26:46 +0200,
Kristof Pelckmans wrote:
> 
> As I understand, all Delta cards are supported that have the Envy24
> chipset.

not all but most of them.

> Is this also true for the Delta 410 ? Does anyone have any
> experience using this card under Linux ? 

it's not supported on alsa yet.

even it using an ice1712 chip, we need the other important information
such like the mixer soundchips and its connection.
otherwise you cannot hear anything.


> Would I be able to drive all my 9 outputs at the same time using
> different inputs ? 
 
iirc, it's partly possible by a certain configuration.
but perhaps it's more difficult to set up it than you imagine...


> Is anyone doing the same thing, maybe using a different card ?
 
no.

> Are there alternative cards to the Delta 410 that have better linux
> support and are worth considering ?
 
other delta cards?  terratec ones are also well supported (except for
DMX 6fire - only analog outputs work so far)


> Would it be possible to get 5 old sound cards and combine them into
> one system without getting interrupt conflicts etc.

five isa cards are almost impossible, because they hog too much
resource.  pci wouldn't be a problem.


